00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:06,520
Completely.

240
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:12,660
When you try to calculate the interaction of gravitons at incredibly small distances, the equations spit out infinities.

241
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:15,300
Infinite energy, infinite probability.

242
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,840
The theory is what we call non-renormalizable.

243
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:19,000
It just breaks.

244
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,680
It's like trying to divide by zero on a calculator.

245
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,620
You just get a big error message.

246
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:24,380
Exactly.

247
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:27,260
And for decades, physicists tried to fix this and failed.

248
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:32,300
But in 1977, Stel made a monumental mathematical discovery.

249
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:39,660
He found that if you modify Einstein's equations, specifically if you add quadratic curvature terms to the action.

250
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:40,160
Hang on.

251
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:40,920
Let's define that.

252
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:42,940
What is a quadratic curvature term?

253
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:43,300
Sure.

254
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:49,400
General relativity is based on space-time curvature, represented by the Ricci scalar, which is a linear term.

255
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:52,020
It's essentially the first derivative of the metric.

256
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:58,360
Stel decided to add terms that are squared, the square of the Ricci scalar and the square of something called the whale tensor.

257
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:02,540
He introduced higher order derivatives into the fundamental equations of gravity.

258
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:04,140
Okay, so he squared some stuff.

259
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:04,460
Right.

260
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:09,220
And when he ran the calculations for this new quadratic gravity, a miracle happened.

261
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:11,340
The equation stopped spinning out infinities.

262
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:13,860
The theory became perfectly renormalizable.

263
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,700
The infinities were entirely cured.

264
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:24,280
Okay, so a guy in 1977 completely solved the infinity problem of quantum gravity by just squaring some of the curvature terms.

265
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:26,140
That sounds like the Holy Grail.

266
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:28,320
That should be Einstein-level famous.

267
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:32,200
Why aren't we all taught Stel's quadratic gravity in high school?

268
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,820
Because of the fatal flaw.

269
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:40,100
When you add those higher derivative terms, you fundamentally change the particle spectrum of the theory.

270
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:47,140
In standard Einstein gravity, you have the graviton, a massless spin-to particle that carries the gravitational force.

271
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:53,040
When Stel added the quadratic terms, the math still produced the massless graviton, which was great.

272
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:53,340
What?

273
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,260
But it also birthed a monster.

274
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:59,320
It created a massive spin-to propagating degree of freedom.

275
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:07,300
And when you look at the kinetic energy term for this new massive particle in the equations, it has a massive negative sign in front of it.

276
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:09,920
The negative kinetic energy, meaning what physically?

277
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:11,660
Think about a ball rolling down a hill.

278
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:16,800
Positive kinetic energy means if you push the ball, it speeds up in the direction you pushed it.

279
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:21,320
A particle with a negative kinetic term, a ghost, behaves inversely.

280
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:23,620
If you push it forward, it accelerates backward.

281
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:24,500
It's bizarre.

282
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,040
It is.

283
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:30,160
If it emits radiation, instead of losing energy and slowing down, it gains energy and speeds up.

284
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Furthermore, when you translate this into quantum mechanics via canonical quantization, this negative kinetic term forces the particle's quantum states to have a negative inner product.

285
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:43,860
It creates a state with a negative probability.

286
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:44,360
Yes.

287
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:48,540
The ghost states represent a negative probability of existence.

288
00:16:49,360 --> 00:17:03,420
So standard physics looked at Stel's brilliant cure for quantum gravity, saw the massive spin-to ghost with its negative probability, invoked the Hilbert assumption, and said negative probability is an observable pathology.

289
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:07,660
It is unphysical, therefore the entire theory is dead on arrival.

290
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:08,160
Wow.

291
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:12,660
And they threw quadratic gravity straight in the theoretical trash can.

292
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:17,800
They discarded the literal cure for quantum gravity because they couldn't handle the ghost in the ledger.

293
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:21,880
They just assumed the negative math would inevitably leak into the physical world.

294
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:31,940
But Flyxion's paper highlights a massive, decades-long rescue operation, right, a way to save stealth theory, spearheaded recently by physicists Neil Turok and Sam Bateman.

295
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:32,500
That's right.

296
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:37,880
And their solution involves abandoning the Hilbert space entirely and moving into something called a crane space.

297
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:41,780
So what is a crane space mathematically, and how does it save the ghost?

298
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:46,540
A crane space is a mathematical arena that explicitly rejects the Hilbert assumption.

299
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:49,440
It is an indefinite inner product space.

300
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:58,900
Unlike a Hilbert space, which violently demands that every single vector have a positive length and a positive probability, a crane space is completely relaxed.

301
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:05,160
It is perfectly happy to contain a positive norm sector and a negative norm sector simultaneously.

302
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:07,280
Okay, but how does that actually help?

303
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:13,400
If you just mathematically allow the negative probability to exist, you haven't solved the physical absurdity.

304
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,860
You still have a negative probability.

305
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:19,340
To see the mechanics of that, we have to look at Neil Turok's brilliant analogy.

306
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:24,800
Think of Winkowski spacetime, the geometric foundation of Einstein's special relativity.

307
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:29,740
In four-dimensional spacetime, we have three dimensions of space and one dimension of time.

308
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:32,580
And crucially, they are mathematically distinct.

309
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:35,640
Spacelike vectors have a positive length squared.

310
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:38,540
Timelike vectors have a negative length squared.

311
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:39,340
Oh, interesting.

312
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:43,540
So the geometry of the universe actually already uses indefinite metrics.

313
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,380
Exactly.

314
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:47,860
Spacetime itself is an indefinite metric space.

315
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:52,600
Spacetime isn't broken just because the time direction has a negative sign in the metric.

316
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:55,560
It just means time behaves differently than space.

317
00:18:56,360 --> 00:19:01,000
Turok and Bateman apply that exact same logic to the quantum state space.

318
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,240
So they treat it like geometry.

319
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:02,940
Yes.

320
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:08,360
A crane space is just a quantum algebra that acknowledges time-like and space-like quantum states.

321
00:19:08,780 --> 00:19:11,060
The positive norm states are standard particles.

322
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,440
The negative norm states are the ghosts.

323
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:19,160
And they are both perfectly valid, well-behaved coordinates internally in the mathematical space.

324
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:21,080
But I'm still stuck on the ATM analogy.

325
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:24,780
The accountant can use the negative numbers in the Crean space ledger.

326
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:30,920
But eventually, the physicist has to calculate an observable physical event like two particles colliding in a collider.

327
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:32,320
They have to go to the ATM.

328
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:38,860
If your equation spits out a negative probability state, a ghost, how does the universe just ignore it?

329
00:19:38,860 --> 00:19:42,640
How do you get a positive, sensible physical probability out of a Crean space?

330
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:45,900
This is the crux of the entire rescue operation.

331
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:51,660
This is what Flyxion formalizes as the observable admissibility theorem.

332
00:19:53,180 --> 00:20:00,440
Turok and Bateman realized that the physicists in the 1970s were calculating probabilities entirely wrong.

333
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:01,260
Oh, so.

334
00:20:01,260 --> 00:20:04,300
In standard quantum mechanics, you use the Born rule.

335
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:10,300
You take the amplitude of a state and you square it, and you basically ignore anything that doesn't physically exist.

336
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:15,580
The 70s physicists tried to just delete the ghost states from the math before doing the calculation,

337
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:19,600
trying to artificially force the Crean space back into a Hilbert space.

338
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:24,120
But when you just arbitrarily delete a mathematically necessary part of the equation,

339
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:28,820
you break the theory's internal symmetries, and the probabilities stop adding up to 100%.

340
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:30,760
It ruins the unitarity of the theory.

341
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:34,060
So you can't just cross the negative numbers out of the ledger with a Sharpie.

342
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:35,680
The books literally won't balance.

343
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:36,000
Right.

344
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,360
So Turok and Bateman modified the approach.

345
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:39,660
They said, leave the ghosts in.

346
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,360
Trace over the entire space.

347
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:43,540
But, and this is the genius part,

348
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:48,840
they identified a hidden mathematical symmetry in quadratic gravity called ghost parity symmetry.

349
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:50,440
Ghost parity symmetry.

350
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:53,180
Okay, let's break down the mechanics of that.

351
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:53,960
How does it work?

352
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:56,420
Imagine a perfectly balanced equation,

353
00:20:56,820 --> 00:21:02,340
where every time a regular positive energy particle interacts and moves forward in time,

354
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:08,100
its negative ghost counterpart mirrors that mathematical action perfectly in the background.

355
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:12,680
Because they are locked in this perfectly symmetrical dance under the rules of the theory,

356
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:17,020
a positive state can never spontaneously mix with a negative state.

357
00:21:17,820 --> 00:21:23,660
The symmetry acts as an impenetrable firewall between the positive norm sector and the negative norm sector.

358
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:26,600
So they exist in the exact same mathematical universe,

359
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:30,180
but they can never physically touch or convert into one another.

360
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:30,700
Exactly.

361
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:34,640
The time evolution of the system strictly commutes with this parity operator.

362
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:41,100
And because of this firewall, the observable admissibility theorem proves a stunning mathematical fact.

363
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:45,340
If you calculate the transition probability of a physical event,

364
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:47,900
and you leave the ghosts fully engaged in the math,

365
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:52,940
the negative contributions of the ghosts will always perfectly cancel out any mathematical anomalies,

366
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:56,240
and the final observable probability will always be positive.

367
00:21:56,780 --> 00:21:57,700
Wait, really?

368
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:01,640
And it will always sum up perfectly to unity 100%.

369
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,700
That is beautiful.

370
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:04,980
The math processes the negative ghost,

371
00:22:05,420 --> 00:22:09,200
uses it to carry the necessary information to cancel out the infinities of gravity,

372
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:11,660
but because of the ghost parity firewall,

373
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:15,200
by the time the calculation reaches the observable output,

374
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:18,020
the negativity has perfectly washed itself out.

375
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:18,540
Yes.

376
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:22,720
And this requires us to deeply internalize the difference between

377
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:27,540
what Flyxion calls a coordinate pathology and an observable pathology.

378
00:22:27,540 --> 00:22:30,800
A coordinate pathology is a glitch, a weird feature,

379
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:33,780
or a negative sign in the internal mathematical map.

380
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:34,680
Like the ledger.

381
00:22:34,820 --> 00:22:35,460
Like the ledger.

382
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:38,780
An observable pathology is when the physical universe actually breaks

383
00:22:38,780 --> 00:22:41,240
like a negative probability of an event happening in a lab.

384
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:46,560
Flyxion argues, conclusively, that a ghost is merely a coordinate pathology.

385
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:50,200
It is a hidden mathematical direction in the admissibility manifold.

386
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:52,240
It does the heavy lifting in the background,

387
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:54,680
but it never bleeds into physical reality.

388
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:59,560
So the physicists in the 1970s threw away the literal cure for quantum gravity

389
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:03,460
because they confused a coordinate glitch for an observable catastrophe.

390
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:06,340
They looked at a negative number in the internal ledger

391
00:23:06,340 --> 00:23:09,080
and assumed the ATM was going to start spitting out antimatter.

392
00:23:09,580 --> 00:23:11,860
They mistook the map for the territory.

393
00:23:12,180 --> 00:23:14,500
That is the exact argument this paper is making.

394
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:17,280
The ghost was never a threat to reality.

395
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:19,840
It was just a feature of the internal math.

396
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:21,560
Okay, the math checks out for probabilities.

397
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:22,560
We solved the ghost.

398
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:25,880
But if I'm tracking the history of physics correctly,

399
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:29,420
negative probabilities aren't the only mathematical monster

400
00:23:29,420 --> 00:23:31,280
hiding in these higher derivative theories.

401
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:33,880
Probabilities are just one part of the equation.

402
00:23:34,380 --> 00:23:35,260
What about energy?

403
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:39,160
Because there is an older, much scarier mathematical theorem

404
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:41,240
from way back in the 19th century that says

405
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:44,820
adding these squared derivatives won't just mess up your probabilities.

406
00:23:44,820 --> 00:23:48,440
It will literally rip the universe apart with infinite energy.

407
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:51,560
Ah, yes, the Ostrogradsky instability.

408
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:54,440
It is the great phantom menace of theoretical physics.

409
00:23:55,340 --> 00:24:00,160
It has been used as a club to beat down higher derivative theories for almost 200 years.

410
00:24:00,560 --> 00:24:01,600
Let's set the stage here.

411
00:24:02,260 --> 00:24:07,380
Who was Ostrogradsky and what mathematical curse did he unleash in 1850?

412
00:24:07,860 --> 00:24:10,860
Mikhail Ostrogradsky was a brilliant Russian mathematician.

413
00:24:10,860 --> 00:24:17,260
In 1850, he proved a highly robust, mathematically unassailable theorem in classical mechanics.

414
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:22,880
He showed that any physical system whose equations rely on irreducible higher-order derivatives,

415
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:28,260
meaning derivatives higher than the first order, like acceleration or the quadratic terms

416
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:33,260
in Stel's gravity, will inherently possess a Hamiltonian that is unbounded below.

417
00:24:33,260 --> 00:24:34,280
Okay, let's unpack that.

418
00:24:34,380 --> 00:24:34,960
The Hamiltonian.

419
00:24:35,060 --> 00:24:40,700
In physics, the Hamiltonian is essentially the master equation for the total energy of a system, correct?

420
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:41,380
Exactly.

421
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:42,920
It represents the total energy.

422
00:24:43,260 --> 00:24:48,060
In a normal, healthy, physical system, the Hamiltonian has a floor, a ground state.

423
00:24:48,140 --> 00:24:51,660
The energy can't go to low zero or at least below some minimum value.

424
00:24:52,060 --> 00:24:54,780
But Ostrogradsky proved that if your equations have higher derivatives,

425
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:58,740
the momentum of the system becomes linearly dependent on those higher derivatives.

426
00:24:58,740 --> 00:25:03,220
And because it's a linear dependence, you can push the energy arbitrarily far into the negative.

427
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:04,380
There is no bottom floor.

428
00:25:04,580 --> 00:25:06,320
The Hamiltonian is unbounded below.

429
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:09,600
It can plunge infinitely toward negative infinity.

430
00:25:09,820 --> 00:25:14,480
And what is the actual physical consequence of an energy state with no bottom floor?

431
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:15,940
Well, in isolation, nothing.

432
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:17,960
But the universe isn't isolated.

433
00:25:18,440 --> 00:25:19,220
Things interact.

434
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:22,100
The standard physics interpretation is catastrophic.

435
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:27,280
If you take a normal system, say, standard electromagnetic fields with positive energy,

436
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:31,420
and you couple it to an Ostrogradsky system like higher derivative gravity,

437
00:25:32,060 --> 00:25:34,500
you get a runaway infinite energy exchange.

438
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:35,320
Like a cascade.

439
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:36,760
A catastrophic cascade.

440
00:25:37,020 --> 00:25:37,200
Yeah.

441
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:39,860
Because the Ostrogradsky system has no bottom floor,

442
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:42,540
it can drop infinitely downward into negative energy.

443
00:25:42,780 --> 00:25:47,140
And because of the strict conservation of total energy for every unit of negative energy it drops,

444
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:51,060
it pumps a unit of positive infinite energy into the normal system.

445
00:25:51,420 --> 00:25:54,340
The higher derivative system plunges to negative infinity,

446
00:25:54,340 --> 00:25:56,640
the normal system shoots up to positive infinity,

447
00:25:56,920 --> 00:26:02,000
and the universe instantly vaporizes in a runaway explosion of infinite heat and radiation.

448
00:26:02,380 --> 00:26:03,760
Well, I mean, I don't know about you,

449
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:08,800
but I feel like I would have noticed if the universe had vaporized in a cascade of infinite energy.

450
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:11,580
That definitely sounds like an observable pathology.

451
00:26:11,940 --> 00:26:16,360
You can't just sweep infinite explosive energy under the rug with a clever probability trick.

452
00:26:16,360 --> 00:26:22,600
So how on earth does Flyxion's framework survive 170-year-old mathematical proof

453
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:25,040
that their theory should instantly destroy the universe?

454
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:32,400
You survive it by applying the exact same coordinate versus observable lens that we just used for the ghosts.

455
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:39,120
You have to look at what Ostrogradsky actually proved versus what physicists merely assumed he proved.

456
00:26:39,760 --> 00:26:43,100
Flyxion explains this through a concept he calls the trajectory shift.

457
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:44,780
What's the trajectory shift?

458
00:26:44,780 --> 00:26:48,900
You see, Ostrogradsky made a mathematical claim about the phase space of the system.

459
00:26:49,580 --> 00:26:52,980
Phase space is the vast, multidimensional mathematical arena

460
00:26:52,980 --> 00:26:56,200
of all potentially possible states a system could occupy,

461
00:26:56,580 --> 00:26:58,340
regardless of the actual laws of motion.

462
00:26:58,880 --> 00:27:02,100
But observable physics isn't about the whole phase space.

463
00:27:02,460 --> 00:27:06,260
It is about the actual histories or trajectories that the dynamics generate over time,

464
00:27:06,580 --> 00:27:08,220
based on actual initial conditions.

465
00:27:08,380 --> 00:27:10,800
I'm going to need a strong analogy to visualize this.

466
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:14,080
I'm thinking about a roller coaster.

467
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:18,940
Let's say Ostrogradsky is a hyper-pedantic safety inspector

468
00:27:18,940 --> 00:27:23,880
looking at a mathematical blueprint of a completely wild new roller coaster.

469
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:24,680
Okay, I'm waiting.

470
00:27:24,740 --> 00:27:27,120
And he points the equations of the blueprint and says,

471
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:29,320
look, according to this math,

472
00:27:29,400 --> 00:27:33,200
the track technically extends infinitely down into the bedrock of the earth.

473
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:35,320
It's an unbounded phase space.

474
00:27:35,840 --> 00:27:39,420
The cart has the mathematical potential to plunge to the center of the planet.

475
00:27:39,640 --> 00:27:44,060
But as the person actually strapped into the cart riding the roller coaster,

476
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,320
I'm sitting there saying it doesn't matter where the theoretical blueprint could go.

477
00:27:47,660 --> 00:27:51,040
The actual physical cart is locked onto a specific dynamic loop.

478
00:27:51,420 --> 00:27:55,500
The laws of momentum and the track design strictly dictate its trajectory.

479
00:27:55,500 --> 00:27:58,560
